  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f2bed5e614b0dd34485c43fa9f9413fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 02_StartingTheTest
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  subject: Starting the Test
  sender: Message
  content: "Dear Student,\n\r\nI\u2019m not sure whether you\u2019ve been diligently
    assembling the cell or just standing blankly in front of the terminal\r\nwaiting
    for my emails\u2014but if you\u2019ve completed the assembly: well done!\n\r\nWe\u2019ve
    had some hiccups with the docking stations in the past (loose cables, overheating,
    the usual), but yours\r\nshould be in working order. To initiate the test, use
    the pad attached directly to the testing chamber. Normally,\r\nyou\u2019d set
    the parameters at a separate terminal, but that interface is currently out of
    order. So, we\u2019ve rerouted\r\neverything through the chamber pad\u2014convenient,
    right?\n\r\nNow pay close attention: once the cell is inserted and the oven door
    is closed, you must form the cell before\r\nstarting the test. I cannot stress
    this enough. If we burn out another cell because someone skipped this step, I\r\nmay
    lose what little composure I have left.\n\r\nOnce the cell is formed, start the
    test. The system will automatically analyze the data for you.\n\r\nOh\u2014and
    here\u2019s a neat trick: if you press \"Reset\" on the machine, it\u2019ll activate
    a built-in time-loop feature, sending\r\nyou and the cell back to just before
    the first testing cycle. Handy for undoing mistakes!\n\r\nKeep going\u2014you\u2019re
    almost there.\n\r\nYour favorite docent,\n\r\nH. Graunt"
  maxMailSize: 220
